# Readability and comments

- Prefer clear names and small functions so intent is obvious without heavy comments.
- Add comments for non-obvious logic, edge cases, and business constraints (the "why"), not line-by-line narration (the "what").
- Keep comments short and maintainable; remove stale comments when code changes.
- Avoid dead code and large commented-out blocks.
- Keep formatting consistent and avoid deeply nested logic when a helper function improves readability.

